<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  CubeGM open-source frontend — RK3036G autorun overlay.

  The stock device stores its settings in cubegm/setting.xml and boots via the
  <autorun> field. The stock value ships EMPTY: <autorun file="" driver="" />.
  This overlay sets it so the device hands control to our frontend instead of
  (or before) the stock menu — WITHOUT touching any stock binary or root.dat,
  so the boot checksum ("sdcard is damaged") is never triggered.

  Mechanism (verified against treefrog-ui/hijack/tfhijack.c):
    driver=""  -> rkgame resolves the core by the ROM's extension.
    dummy.md   -> .md  -> rkgame dlopens cubegm/cores/libemu_md.so
                  (which we install as our libemu_tfhijack.so, renamed).
    tfhijack forks zhijack.sh -> picoarch + FrogUI.

  Place this file at cubegm/setting.xml (it REPLACES the stock setting.xml;
  the open-source frontend only needs the <autorun> field to boot). If you want
  to keep the device's existing language/volume/sound settings, instead MERGE
  only the <autorun .../> line below into the device's existing
  cubegm/setting.xml.
-->
<setting>
  <autorun file="/mnt/sdcard/MD/dummy.md" driver="" />
</setting>
